{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Looped vertices are removed and each connected component solved alone. A bipartite","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component costs O(m √n): a maximum matching (Hopcroft–Karp), the alternating reach from its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"free vertices (König), and one pass over the perfectly matched core along the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dulmage–Mendelsohn implications. A complete component takes its least vertex. Any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"component is solved once: the degree-0, -1 and -2 reductions (taking a leaf, folding a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degree-2 vertex), then, on the kernel’s non-bipartite components, branch and bound on bitset","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rows of the complement with a greedy-colouring bound (BBMC; San Segundo et al. 2011). O(n +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"m) plus the search on what the reductions leave, exponential in the kernel’s size in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"worst case. Memory O(n + m + k² \/ 64) words for a kernel component of k vertices. The search","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum independent set (exact), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. A vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once. Deterministic, but which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"maximum set it is depends on the search; for one fixed by a rule, see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE21maximumIndependentSetSay6VertexQzGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1669"},"title":"maximumIndependentSet()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumindependentset()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumIndependentSet()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Covering/do